  },
  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Job",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 41,
    "summary": "The Lord points to His power in the leviathan—All things under the whole heaven are the Lord’s.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Canst thou draw out leviathan with an hook? or his tongue with a cord which thou lettest down?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 70,
            "end": 75
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 41:1",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 41,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "Canst thou put an hook into his nose? or bore his jaw through with a thorn?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 41:2",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 41,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "Will he make many supplications unto thee? will he speak soft words unto thee?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 62,
            "end": 67
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 41:3",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 41,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "Will he make a covenant with thee? wilt thou take him for a servant for ever?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 41:4",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 41,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "Wilt thou play with him as with a bird? or wilt thou bind him for thy maidens?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 27,
            "end": 31
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 41:5",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 41,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "Shall the companions make a banquet of him? shall they part him among the merchants?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 41:6",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 41,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "Canst thou fill his skin with barbed irons? or his head with fish spears?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 30,
            "end": 42,
            "text": "OR harpoons."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 41:7",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 41,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "Lay thine hand upon him, remember the battle, do no more.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 41:8",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 41,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "Behold, the hope of him is in vain: shall not one be cast down even at the sight of him?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 46,
            "end": 49
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 41:9",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 41,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "None is so fierce that dare stir him up: who then is able to stand before me?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 5,
            "end": 10
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 41:10",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 41,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "Who hath prevented me, that I should repay him? whatsoever is under the whole heaven is mine.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 43,
            "end": 61
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 41:11",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 41,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "I will not conceal his parts, nor his power, nor his comely proportion.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 41:12",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 41,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "Who can discover the face of his garment? or who can come to him with his double bridle?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 42,
            "end": 44
          },
          {
            "start": 58,
            "end": 64
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 41:13",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 41,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "Who can open the doors of his face? his teeth are terrible round about.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 46,
            "end": 49
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 41:14",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 41,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "His scales are his pride, shut up together as with a close seal.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 3
          },
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 18
          },
          {
            "start": 43,
            "end": 50
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 41:15",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 41,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "One is so near to another, that no air can come between them.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 41:16",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 41,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "They are joined one to another, they stick together, that they cannot be sundered.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 17,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 41:17",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 41,
        "verse": 17
      },
      {
        "text": "By his neesings a light doth shine, and his eyes are like the eyelids of the morning.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 7,
            "end": 15,
            "text": "OR sneezings."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 49,
            "end": 52
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 18,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 41:18",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 41,
        "verse": 18
      },
      {
        "text": "Out of his mouth go burning lamps, and sparks of fire leap out.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 35,
            "end": 38
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 19,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 41:19",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 41,
        "verse": 19
      },
      {
        "text": "Out of his nostrils goeth smoke, as out of a seething pot or caldron.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 36,
            "end": 39
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 20,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 41:20",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 41,
        "verse": 20
      },
      {
        "text": "His breath kindleth coals, and a flame goeth out of his mouth.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 21,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 41:21",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 41,
        "verse": 21
      },
      {
        "text": "In his neck remaineth strength, and sorrow is turned into joy before him.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 22,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 41:22",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 41,
        "verse": 22
      },
      {
        "text": "The flakes of his flesh are joined together: they are firm in themselves; they cannot be moved.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 23,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 41:23",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 41,
        "verse": 23
      },
      {
        "text": "His heart is as firm as a stone; yea, as hard as a piece of the nether millstone.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 71,
            "end": 81
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 24,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 41:24",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 41,
        "verse": 24
      },
      {
        "text": "When he raiseth up himself, the mighty are afraid: by reason of breakings they purify themselves.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 25,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 41:25",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 41,
        "verse": 25
      },
      {
        "text": "The sword of him that layeth at him cannot hold: the spear, the dart, nor the habergeon.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 26,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 41:26",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 41,
        "verse": 26
      },
      {
        "text": "He esteemeth iron as straw, and brass as rotten wood.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 28,
            "end": 31
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 27,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 41:27",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 41,
        "verse": 27
      },
      {
        "text": "The arrow cannot make him flee: slingstones are turned with him into stubble.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 28,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 41:28",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 41,
        "verse": 28
      },
      {
        "text": "Darts are counted as stubble: he laugheth at the shaking of a spear.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 29,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 41:29",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 41,
        "verse": 29
      },
      {
        "text": "Sharp stones are under him: he spreadeth sharp pointed things upon the mire.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 13,
            "end": 16
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 30,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 41:30",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 41,
        "verse": 30
      },
      {
        "text": "He maketh the deep to boil like a pot: he maketh the sea like a pot of ointment.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 31,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 41:31",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 41,
        "verse": 31
      },
      {
        "text": "He maketh a path to shine after him; one would think the deep to be hoary.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 37,
            "end": 40
          },
          {
            "start": 62,
            "end": 67
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 32,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 41:32",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 41,
        "verse": 32
      },
      {
        "text": "Upon earth there is not his like, who is made without fear.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 33,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 41:33",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 41,
        "verse": 33
      },
      {
        "text": "He beholdeth all high things: he is a king over all the children of pride.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 22,
            "end": 29
          },
          {
            "start": 33,
            "end": 35
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 34,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 41:34",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 41,
        "verse": 34
      }
    ]
  },
